  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_FACTOR_PASS. F-NET-PAYOUT-YIELD-US used 61 point-in-time first-release Federal Reserve Z.1 quarterly observations from 2011Q1 through 2026Q1 and defined risk-on as the latest net payout yield being at or above the prior-only expanding median. It produced CAGR 14.321400%, Sharpe 1.518323 and MDD 7.689054%, slightly below frozen V11 on CAGR and Sharpe while preserving the same maximum drawdown. It beat its availability-matched unconditional retention control on full Sharpe (1.518323 versus 1.496986) but not on CAGR and beat matched-control Sharpe in only 3/7 fixed folds. Paired 63-session moving-block bootstrap over 20000 replicates gave P(CAGR candidate > V11)=36.120% and P(Sharpe candidate > matched)=81.525%; median candidate-minus-V11 CAGR was negative while median candidate-minus-matched Sharpe was positive. Candidate MDD P97.5=14.035% passed the 15% risk ceiling. Cumulative 30-trial DSR probability was 94.241%, below the frozen 95% requirement. The factor therefore does not qualify for factor-library validated/promotion publication. Per the frozen stop rule, no fixed threshold, rolling percentile, q/q or y/y transformation, payout-component variant, denominator/normalization, sign reversal, retention-fraction or second retrospective Net Payout search is permitted.",
